\PYG{n}{decomposition\PYGZus{}prompt} \PYG{o}{=} \PYG{l+s+sa}{f}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}\PYGZdq{}\PYGZdq{}}\PYG{l+s+se}{\PYGZbs{}}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{        Given a set of dataset columns, a ground\PYGZhy{}truth hypothesis, and the analysis workflow used, your task is to extract the set of sub\PYGZhy{}hypotheses that are present in the hypothesis such that each sub\PYGZhy{}hypothesis covers a separate context, is self\PYGZhy{}sufficient, and operates on a coherent set of 3 dimensions: Context, Variables, and Relations.}

\PYG{l+s+s2}{        Here are the definitions for these dimensions:}

\PYG{l+s+s2}{        \PYGZhy{} Contexts: Boundary conditions that limit the scope of a sub\PYGZhy{}hypothesis. E.g., “for men over the age of 30”, “in Asia and Europe”, or \PYGZdq{}None\PYGZdq{} if there is no boundary condition specified.}

\PYG{l+s+s2}{        \PYGZhy{} Variables: Known concepts that interact in a meaningful way under a given context to produce the sub\PYGZhy{}hypothesis. E.g., gender, age, income, or \PYGZdq{}None\PYGZdq{} if there is no interacting variable.}

\PYG{l+s+s2}{        \PYGZhy{} Relations: Interactions between a given set of variables under a given context to produce the sub\PYGZhy{}hypothesis. E.g., “quadratic relationship”, “inversely proportional”, piecewise conditionals, or \PYGZdq{}None\PYGZdq{} if there is no interacting relationship.}

\PYG{l+s+s2}{        Make sure to only use the information present in the hypothesis and the workflow. Do not add any new information.}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{        If no sub\PYGZhy{}hypotheses can be extracted, return an empty list.}

\PYG{l+s+s2}{        Here is the metadata for the task:}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{        ```json}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{        }\PYG{l+s+se}{\PYGZob{}\PYGZob{}}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{            \PYGZdq{}datasets\PYGZdq{}: }\PYG{l+s+si}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n}{dataset\PYGZus{}metadata}\PYG{l+s+si}{\PYGZcb{}}\PYG{l+s+s2}{,}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{            \PYGZdq{}hypothesis\PYGZdq{}: \PYGZdq{}}\PYG{l+s+si}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n}{hypothesis}\PYG{l+s+si}{\PYGZcb{}}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{},}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{            \PYGZdq{}workflow\PYGZdq{}: \PYGZdq{}}\PYG{l+s+si}{\PYGZob{}}\PYG{n}{workflow}\PYG{l+s+si}{\PYGZcb{}}\PYG{l+s+s2}{\PYGZdq{}}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{        }\PYG{l+s+se}{\PYGZcb{}\PYGZcb{}}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{        ```}

\PYG{l+s+s2}{        Return your answer as a JSON object in the following format:}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{        ```json}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{        }\PYG{l+s+se}{\PYGZob{}\PYGZob{}}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{        \PYGZdq{}sub\PYGZus{}hypo\PYGZdq{}: [}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{            }\PYG{l+s+se}{\PYGZob{}\PYGZob{}}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{                \PYGZdq{}text\PYGZdq{}: the sub\PYGZhy{}hypothesis in natural language,}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{                \PYGZdq{}context\PYGZdq{}: a short text description of the context of the sub\PYGZhy{}hypothesis,}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{                \PYGZdq{}variables\PYGZdq{}: a list of columns involved in the sub\PYGZhy{}hypothesis,}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{                \PYGZdq{}relations\PYGZdq{}: a short text description of the relationship between the variables of the sub\PYGZhy{}hypothesis,}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{                \PYGZdq{}explanation\PYGZdq{}: a short text explanation for the breakdown of the sub\PYGZhy{}hypothesis}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{            }\PYG{l+s+se}{\PYGZcb{}\PYGZcb{}}\PYG{l+s+s2}{,}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{            ...}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{        ]}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{        }\PYG{l+s+se}{\PYGZcb{}\PYGZcb{}}\PYG{l+s+s2}{```}
\PYG{l+s+s2}{        \PYGZdq{}\PYGZdq{}\PYGZdq{}}
